# {{ project_name }}

A Fyso Agentic Framework project: OpenMausBot (bots) + Dagu (workflows) behind one gateway.

## Run it

Requirements: Git, [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev), and authenticated Claude Code / Codex CLIs for the corresponding bots. Framework tools are pinned in `mise.toml`. Initialize and commit this generated project before starting the stack.

[Repository installation guide](https://github.com/fyso-dev/agentic-framework/blob/preview/docs/installation.md) covers generation, prerequisites, updates and recovery.

```sh
mise trust && mise install
mise run setup     # once: your age key + encrypted secrets (login admin / admin)
mise run up
```

| What | Where |
|---|---|
| Panel | http://panel.localhost:{{ port_base }} |
| Dagu (workflows) | http://dagu.localhost:{{ port_base }} |
| OpenMausBot (bots) | http://omb.localhost:{{ port_base }} (project login, no pairing code) |

`mise run doctor` checks everything · `mise run status` · `mise run logs <dagu|omb|caddy>` · `mise run down`

## Where things live

| Path | Owner | What |
|---|---|---|
| `project/` | this project | bots, workflows, apps — yours to change |
| `framework/` | template | updated with `uvx copier update --trust`; do not edit |
| `secrets.enc.yaml` | this project | encrypted with sops + age; edit with `mise run secrets` |
| `.data/` | runtime | data of Dagu, OpenMausBot and Caddy; never committed |

Ports {{ port_base }}–{{ port_base + 9 }} belong to this project. This project never connects to another Dagu or OpenMausBot on the machine.

## Build a change

Ask the Builder bot in OpenMausBot, or start `fyso-dev-task` in Dagu with:

- `TASK`: the requested change and acceptance criteria.
- `PROVIDER`: `claude` (default) or `codex`, using the host CLI login.
- `BASE`: an existing local branch (`main` by default).
- `BRANCH`: optional feature branch; otherwise `builder/<run-id>`.
- `MODEL`: optional provider model.
- `PUBLISH`: `false` by default; `true` pushes to `origin` and opens a PR with `gh`.

The workflow requires a nonempty change, checks paths and secrets, and runs
`project/check.sh` if that file is executable. That script runs from the candidate
worktree; write it to run your project's tests. A person reviews and merges.
Failures preserve `.data/worktrees/<run-id>` for inspection. Successful runs remove
the worktree and retain the branch. No code change reaches the base branch.

Claude and Codex must already be installed and signed in on the host. Their user
configuration can still affect execution (particularly Codex hooks and skills).

## Observe bots and execution

Open **Observabilidad** in the panel. OMB conversations/delegations, Dagu runs and
structured CLI usage are refreshed every two minutes by `fyso-observability`.
Use the refresh action for an immediate collection. Configure advisory thresholds
and custom engine billing categories in `project/observability.json`; null disables
a threshold. Amounts distinguish reported API USD, subscription equivalents,
estimates and unknowns. No provider invoice reconciliation or automatic stop is
implied. Native history lives in `.data`, survives restart and needs a runtime
backup to survive deletion. It is not included in git memory snapshots.

## Manage bots by conversation

Open OpenMausBot and talk to **Bot Architect**: ask it to create, list, read,
update or delete a project bot. It previews native OMB changes and applies explicit
requests through `fyso-bot-architect`, with snapshots and Git commits before/after.
Ambiguous targets require clarification. Framework/Chief bots cannot be deleted,
and active bots are not interrupted. New bots default to approval `ask`, computer
`off`, and this project's root. The existing panel remains available.

For scripts and diagnostics, the same workflow is available as:

```sh
mise run bots:architect '{"OP":"list"}'
```

Bot snapshots contain imported skill bundles. Ambient skills discovered in the
host CLI remain host-owned; they are not copied into project snapshots. Native
team paths resolve relative to the source file, and instruction placeholders are
preserved. Known home/project paths are normalized in the versioned memory copy.
